{"id": "tea:tirukkural:1", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "1", "verse": "1", "chapter": "1 (Kaṭavuḷ vāḻttu, praise of God)"}, "paraphrase": "As the letter 'a' is the first of all letters, so the Primal Lord (Āti Pakavaṉ) is the first of the world.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "disputes": ["dsp:affiliation-of-tirukkural"], "original": {"text": "அகர முதல எழுத்தெல்லாம் ஆதி பகவன் முதற்றே உலகு", "script": "Tamil", "edition": "from memory; to be checked"}, "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:10", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "10", "verse": "10", "chapter": "1"}, "paraphrase": "Those who reach the feet of the Lord cross the great ocean of births; others do not.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "disputes": ["dsp:affiliation-of-tirukkural"], "original": {"text": "பிறவிப் பெருங்கடல் நீந்துவர் நீந்தார் இறைவன் அடிசேரா தார்", "script": "Tamil", "edition": "from memory; to be checked"}, "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:1103", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "1103", "verse": "1103", "chapter": "111 (Puṇarcci makiḻtal, book of love)"}, "paraphrase": "Is the world of the lotus-eyed one sweeter than sleep in the soft arms of the one you love?", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "disputes": ["dsp:affiliation-of-tirukkural"], "notes": "Cited by the Vaiṣṇava side (Viṣṇu's world).", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:2", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "2", "verse": "2", "chapter": "1"}, "paraphrase": "What is the use of learning, if one does not worship the good feet of the one of pure knowledge?", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "ethics"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "disputes": ["dsp:affiliation-of-tirukkural"], "original": {"text": "கற்றதனால் ஆய பயனென்கொல் வாலறிவன் நற்றாள் தொழாஅர் எனின்", "script": "Tamil", "edition": "from memory; to be checked"}, "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:25", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "25", "verse": "25", "chapter": "3 (Nīttār perumai, greatness of renunciants)"}, "paraphrase": "Indra, lord of the dwellers of the wide heaven, is witness to the power of one who has subdued the five senses.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics", "powers-experiences"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "disputes": ["dsp:affiliation-of-tirukkural"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:259", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "259", "verse": "259", "chapter": "26 (Pulāl maṟuttal, abstaining from meat)"}, "paraphrase": "Not to kill and eat a living being is better than pouring ghee into the fire in a thousand sacrifices.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "terms": ["trm:pulal-maruttal"], "practices": ["prc:pulal-maruttal"], "disputes": ["dsp:affiliation-of-tirukkural"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:260", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "260", "verse": "260", "chapter": "26"}, "paraphrase": "All living beings will join their hands in worship of one who neither kills nor eats flesh.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "practices": ["prc:pulal-maruttal"], "disputes": ["dsp:affiliation-of-tirukkural"], "original": {"text": "கொல்லான் புலாலை மறுத்தானைக் கைகூப்பி எல்லா உயிரும் தொழும்", "script": "Tamil", "edition": "from memory; to be checked"}, "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:267", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "267", "verse": "267", "chapter": "27 (Tavam, austerity)"}, "paraphrase": "As gold shines brighter the more it is burned, so the pain of austerity makes those who endure it shine.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "terms": ["trm:tavam"], "practices": ["prc:tapas"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:3", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "3", "verse": "3", "chapter": "1"}, "paraphrase": "Those who reach the glorious feet of the one who walked upon the flower (malarmicai ēkiṉāṉ) will live long on earth.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "disputes": ["dsp:affiliation-of-tirukkural"], "notes": "Read by Jains as the Jina who walks on lotuses, by Śaivas as the Lord in the heart-lotus, by others as Brahmā/Viṣṇu or the Buddha.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:322", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "322", "verse": "322", "chapter": "33 (Kollāmai, non-killing)"}, "paraphrase": "Sharing one's food and protecting all living beings is the foremost of all precepts gathered by the authors of texts.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "practices": ["prc:kollamai"], "terms": ["trm:kollamai"], "original": {"text": "பகுத்துண்டு பல்லுயிர் ஓம்புதல் நூலோர் தொகுத்தவற்றுள் எல்லாம் தலை", "script": "Tamil", "edition": "from memory; to be checked"}, "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:327", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "327", "verse": "327", "chapter": "33"}, "paraphrase": "Do not do what takes another's life, even if it costs you your own.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "practices": ["prc:kollamai"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:336", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "336", "verse": "336", "chapter": "34 (Nilaiyāmai, impermanence)"}, "paraphrase": "'He was here yesterday, he is not today' — such is the greatness of this world.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["death-dying"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:338", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "338", "verse": "338", "chapter": "34"}, "paraphrase": "The bond between body and life is like a bird's that flies away leaving its shell (or nest) empty.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["death-dying", "body-layers"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:339", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "339", "verse": "339", "chapter": "34"}, "paraphrase": "Death is like sleep; birth is like waking from sleep.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["death-dying", "karma-liberation"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "original": {"text": "உறங்குவது போலும் சாக்காடு உறங்கி விழிப்பது போலும் பிறப்பு", "script": "Tamil", "edition": "from memory; to be checked"}, "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:34", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "34", "verse": "34", "chapter": "4 (Aṟaṉ valiyuṟuttal)"}, "paraphrase": "To be spotless in mind is the whole of virtue; all else is empty display.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "terms": ["trm:aram"], "original": {"text": "மனத்துக்கண் மாசிலன் ஆதல் அனைத்தறன் ஆகுல நீர பிற", "script": "Tamil", "edition": "from memory; to be checked"}, "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:346", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "346", "verse": "346", "chapter": "35 (Tuṟavu, renunciation)"}, "paraphrase": "One who destroys the pride of 'I' and 'mine' enters a world higher than the gods'.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "obstacles": ["obs:yan-enatu"], "terms": ["trm:turavu"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:350", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "350", "verse": "350", "chapter": "35"}, "paraphrase": "Cling to the attachment of the One who is without attachment; cling to it so as to let go of attachment.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "original": {"text": "பற்றுக பற்றற்றான் பற்றினை அப்பற்றைப் பற்றுக பற்று விடற்கு", "script": "Tamil", "edition": "from memory; to be checked"}, "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:355", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "355", "verse": "355", "chapter": "36 (Meyyuṇartal, realization of truth)"}, "paraphrase": "Whatever a thing may appear to be, to see its true reality is wisdom.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "terms": ["trm:meyyunartal"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:358", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "358", "verse": "358", "chapter": "36"}, "paraphrase": "Wisdom is to see the true reality called 'excellence' (ciṟappu, release), so that the folly called birth departs.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "terms": ["trm:cemporul", "trm:vitu"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:360", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "360", "verse": "360", "chapter": "36"}, "paraphrase": "When desire, anger and delusion — even their names — are destroyed, suffering is destroyed.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "obstacles": ["obs:kamam-vekuli-mayakkam"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:361", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "361", "verse": "361", "chapter": "37 (Avāvaṟuttal, eradication of desire)"}, "paraphrase": "Desire is the seed that yields, at every time and to every creature, unceasing birth.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "causal", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "obstacles": ["obs:ava"], "terms": ["trm:avavaruttal"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:370", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "370", "verse": "370", "chapter": "37"}, "paraphrase": "If one gives up desire, never satisfied by its nature, that very state gives the unchanging nature.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "obstacles": ["obs:ava"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:380", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "380", "verse": "380", "chapter": "38 (Ūḻ, fate)"}, "paraphrase": "What is stronger than fate (ūḻ)? Even when one devises another way, it comes first.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "causal", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["world-fate"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "terms": ["trm:ul"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:391", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "391", "verse": "391", "chapter": "40 (Kalvi, learning)"}, "paraphrase": "Learn thoroughly what is to be learned, and then live in accordance with it.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "original": {"text": "கற்க கசடறக் கற்பவை கற்றபின் நிற்க அதற்குத் தக", "script": "Tamil", "edition": "from memory; to be checked"}, "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:423", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "423", "verse": "423", "chapter": "43 (Aṟivuṭaimai, wisdom)"}, "paraphrase": "Whatever is heard from whomever, to discern its true meaning is wisdom.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:5", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "5", "verse": "5", "chapter": "1"}, "paraphrase": "The two deeds born of darkness (iruviṉai) do not cling to those who delight in the true praise of the Lord.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "terms": ["trm:iruvinai"], "disputes": ["dsp:affiliation-of-tirukkural"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:6", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "6", "verse": "6", "chapter": "1"}, "paraphrase": "Those who stand in the flawless path of the one who destroyed the five gates of the senses (poṟivāyil aintavittāṉ) will live long.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "disputes": ["dsp:affiliation-of-tirukkural"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:610", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "610", "verse": "610", "chapter": "61 (Maṭiyiṉmai, freedom from sloth)"}, "paraphrase": "The king free of sloth will gain all that was measured by the one who measured the worlds with his feet.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "disputes": ["dsp:affiliation-of-tirukkural"], "notes": "An allusion to Viṣṇu as Trivikrama, cited by the Vaiṣṇava side.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:72", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "72", "verse": "72", "chapter": "8 (Aṉpuṭaimai, love)"}, "paraphrase": "The loveless own everything for themselves; the loving belong to others even to their bones.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "terms": ["trm:anpu"], "original": {"text": "அன்பிலார் எல்லாம் தமக்குரியர் அன்புடையார் என்பும் உரியர் பிறர்க்கு", "script": "Tamil", "edition": "from memory; to be checked"}, "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:8", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "8", "verse": "8", "chapter": "1"}, "paraphrase": "Only those who reach the feet of the gracious one who is the ocean (or wheel) of virtue (aṟavāḻi antaṇaṉ) can cross the other seas.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "disputes": ["dsp:affiliation-of-tirukkural"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:80", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "80", "verse": "80", "chapter": "8"}, "paraphrase": "The body that love inhabits is the seat of life; in those without love it is bone wrapped in skin.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics", "body-layers"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "terms": ["trm:anpu"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:81", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "81", "verse": "81", "chapter": "9 (Viruntōmpal, hospitality)"}, "paraphrase": "The whole purpose of keeping a household and living in it is to cherish guests and do good.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "practices": ["prc:viruntompal"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkural:9", "source": "src:tirukkural", "location": {"ref": "9", "verse": "9", "chapter": "1"}, "paraphrase": "Heads that do not bow to the feet of the one of eight qualities (eṇkuṇattāṉ) are like senses without function.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "teachers": ["tch:tiruvalluvar"], "concepts": ["cpt:eight-qualities-of-siva"], "terms": ["trm:enkunam"], "disputes": ["dsp:affiliation-of-tirukkural"], "notes": "Parimēlaḻakar glosses the eight qualities with Śiva's eight attributes from the Śaiva Āgamas; Jains read them as the eight qualities of a Siddha.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
